Reproducible-computation sources — books, research, and primary manuals (@rc-sources: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @reproducible-computation) { r_7RY36NATQ0VQE5JMJAMF6KXK3K
The reading begins with whole open books and practical exercises, then uses exact primary contracts and research papers to deepen a specific calculation. Sources remain at authorized external locations; no books, papers, downloaded datasets, or dependency/media collections are bundled.

**Sustained books:** [Introduction to Scientific Programming with Python — Sundnes](sources/Scientific-Python-Sundnes.lingua#r_1V7KWH76GSD7XMA9TQVSTEQSWB) supplies a first programming course. [Research Software Engineering with Python — Irving and colleagues](sources/Research-Software-Engineering.lingua#r_07D4PDD4HGKNK3PW4M90YSV2QY) supplies a complete research-software programme and project. [The Good Research Code Handbook — Mineault and community](sources/Good-Research-Code.lingua#r_771ZMSHAY1TCSTFCHPT9KZRA66) develops research practices and numerical testing. [Pro Git — Chacon and Straub](sources/Pro-Git.lingua#r_7NQ43JGJ863RMR0HDHA7GMRD9G) includes a Portuguese translation and a sustained account of distributed version control. [The Unix Shell — Software Carpentry](sources/Unix-Shell.lingua#r_5YJ6K2A69H1D45AADES3QR94AX) supplies practical command-line preparation.

**Research and conceptual work:** [Good enough practices in scientific computing — Wilson and colleagues](sources/Scientific-Computing-Practices.lingua#r_5J8HXCQDNJH59EZC1PRJTQK38B) · [Ten Simple Rules for Reproducible Computational Research — Sandve and colleagues](sources/Reproducible-Research-Rules.lingua#r_5WNPQ4CBNZFM416E5TTNSKKPQG) · [Reproducible Research in Computational Science — Peng](sources/Reproducibility-and-Replication.lingua#r_32SK41ZP8P04Z0PMZX5NN6C2T9) · [What Every Computer Scientist Should Know About Floating-Point Arithmetic — Goldberg](sources/Floating-Point-Goldberg.lingua#r_4FHXH9WWX5Q535CD32ESSVSEHH) · [PROV — entities, activities, and responsibility — W3C](sources/Computational-Provenance.lingua#r_41T4TPCSCESX7SDK9BY4YQZX15) · [FAIR Guiding Principles — Wilkinson and colleagues](sources/FAIR-Principles.lingua#r_1DJWX0MM8DMEK300ZF8PHGQVB9). Read complete papers, then compare their claims with actual reconstruction evidence and the current operation contracts. [The Turing Way — reproducible research, collaboration, and preservation](sources/The-Turing-Way.lingua#r_5K6W3KETGFH4N3SDYCB5V0Q3MZ) supplies a broader connected research handbook; follow its relevant guides as assigned rather than treating it as an external collection to ingest.

**Primary operation and environment references:** [Python tutorial and standard-library references — Python documentation](sources/Python-Reference.lingua#r_53J5SVX9CRECPQJFX3EAD8NRCZ) · [Environments, dependency records, and packaging — PyPA](sources/Python-Environments-and-Packaging.lingua#r_5VVAF04TH8R3DRY9Z36308BH88) · [GNU Make and executable dependency workflows](sources/Make-Workflows.lingua#r_6Y907BH3SMATGCHV3C7ZC2CVMF) · [Workflow graphs, environments, and execution — Snakemake documentation](sources/Snakemake-Workflows.lingua#r_6FGN565JFTD2FTW69KDCS9BWHS) · [Executable notebooks and unattended execution — Jupyter](sources/Executable-Notebooks.lingua#r_0Q66F0CBYJG56Y8KGBGY97X5YN) · [Declarative environments and pinned inputs — Nix documentation](sources/Declarative-Environments.lingua#r_4RZDRCZGB1NQ9119G6RNSWPT2W) · [Containers, base-image identity, and build inputs — Docker documentation](sources/Containers-and-System-Dependencies.lingua#r_6KC0T0B4V0BQ768092K6BN2N4J) · [Deterministic artifacts and environmental variation — Reproducible Builds](sources/Reproducible-Builds.lingua#r_1WZF9P4S3GQYQWVT15HWJVCQ3A) · [Numerical arrays and reproducible random streams — NumPy documentation](sources/Numerical-and-Random-Contracts.lingua#r_22SKS09JTH3YF4244RX2FYWHNY). Source Records identify access, versions or dates, rights information, and any automated-access limits. A linked manual's existence is not evidence that a learner's environment implements every described option.

**Shared sources and learning:** [Data Organization in Spreadsheets — Broman and Woo](../quantitative-literacy/sources/Data-Organization.lingua#r_6AXFG9QT0X74W3DRDE58RP470M), [Quantitative and technical literacy](../quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2), [Measurement and metrology](../metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), and [Propagation of distributions using Monte Carlo — JCGM 101](../metrology/sources/GUM-Monte-Carlo.lingua#r_79V20QP3T2KZ6GD07SK5TGZ1J4) provide the existing mathematical, data, and measurement foundations. The four reused learning Records retain their other continuations and gain a distinct reproducible-computation continuation. References to these roots and books do not add them to the selected learning edges automatically.

Assignments distinguish whole books, whole chapters, exact operation references, and later research reading. Freely accessible and openly licensed are stated separately. Preserve actual edition/component notices when retaining or adapting material. Access and metadata were checked on 29 October 2026 where reachable; specific limitations remain in the relevant source Record.

